Z||000013||Black88GT||04-13-2001||12:07 AM||||Squoach, there is a chemical test that you can have done to see if its your headgasket.  I just know its called a Head Gasket chemical breach test, call around to your local shops and see if they offer it.||||reg||1
Z||000014||sqoach||04-13-2001||12:27 AM||||Kerri, I've never heard of that test, but I'll try it out tomorrow. Seems as though I've done something like that before. The coolant obviously comes out if I take the radiator cap off.<P>Cheev, don't worry about it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>That's just something else for me to check off. I would have probably had that done pretty soon anyway.<P>Black, I'll have to check into that. A bad head gasket would definately be better than a cracked head or block.<P>Thanks everyone. I'll get this problem figured out sooner or later  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||sqoach||04-14-2001||01:17 AM||||Well, I drove around for quite a while tonight. Probably added up to about two hours altogether. My car did just fine the whole time. The only time it got kinda (about 210) was when I stopped to get gas. But that's normal, right? I figured it would do ok after I burped they system, which it always does. Guess I just have to keep driving it to find out, huh?||||reg||1
